      "summary": "Solid first cut. The most important contextual flag for this sign is that Prunus domestica (European plum) is not well-suited to central/south Florida's low-chill winters — UF/IFAS plum cultivation guidance for the state focuses on Japanese-type and 'Gulf'-series cultivars, not P. domestica. The sign reflects this honestly. Butterfly host data (Eastern Tiger Swallowtail) is confirmed by multiple extension sources. Toxicity data from ASPCA and Poison Control is solid.",
